HST Office: ribbon groups and buttons at the geometry of the approved 1.0.2 mockup (large, medium, small, folded).

Owner reports (15/11/2026): a large menu button drew its ▾ beside its icon, "Chọn" (Select) sat higher than the
labels beside it, the icons of Find and Replace were not in one column. Every large button of the ribbon now
follows one geometry, the mockup's (plans/261115-2225-ribbon-mockup-1-0-2/reference/mockup-expected.json):

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonGeometry.hxx (new, plain arithmetic, unit tested): the mockup's sizes in logical px, turned
  into device px once where they are used. A large button (L) is as high as the group's content (76 px), at least
  42 px wide, its icon centred in a 32 px slot 6 px under its top, its label on at most two lines under it,
  split as the mockup's twoLines() (no split for one word or a label of 7 characters at most, else at the space
  that makes the longer line shortest in characters; a one-line label wider than 72 px splits too), ▾ ending the
  second line (alone on it after a one-line label). A medium button (M) is 24 px high, 4 px padding, 5 px between
  icon and label; a small one (S) its icon in 22 px; the ▾ part of a split one 12 px. A folded group's button (C)
  is 98 px high, its name on the caption line.
- toolbox.cxx: the ribbon's tool buttons (owner-drawn notebookbar toolboxes only; every other toolbox is
  unchanged) are measured and drawn at that geometry, whatever the native theme's button borders, so every large
  button puts its icon and the first line of its label at the same height whatever its label; the label's first
  line follows the image after the gap VCL's PushButton leaves, so the large menu buttons (Select ▾) line up too.
- HstRibbonGrid.hxx: the 3-row grid of the medium and small sizes makes ceil(n/3) columns of ceil(n/columns)
  buttons (the mockup's grid(): four buttons are two columns of two, not three and one); a group authored with
  three rows at the large size (its caption in row 3) keeps them; LABEL_WRAP is the 72 px cap.
- HstRibbonLadder.cxx: a large menu button stands at the top of the group's content, its image moved down to the
  large buttons' icon line (WB_TOP, a top margin over its frame's 4 px), as wide as a large tool button with its
  label; large tool boxes stand at the top, medium and small ones at their column's left edge (Find over Replace);
  every group's frame is the mockup's whatever its .ui: 4 px padding, 2 px between columns and rows, the caption
  band 18 px high at the bottom with its text centred (one caption line in every tab of every application), the
  separator 1 px wide, 6 px from the body's top and bottom, 3 px after the content (8 px from content to content,
  the first group's content 4 px inside the page). The caption row of a group is
  its lowest row (2, or 3 for the 3-row columns), holding a label or the box of the label and the launcher.
- HstRibbonPaint: FoldedButtonSize and DrawFoldedButton measure and draw a folded group's "Caption ▾" button for
  PriorityMergedHBox::HstGroupButton (the contract is in HstRibbonPaint.hxx).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
